.el .ds Aq '
.TH export 1  "export " 
.SH NAME
export \- Export the public key of a key file (armored, or a DNS pin record)
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBexport\fR [\fB\-k\fR|\fB\-\-key\fR] [\fB\-o\fR|\fB\-\-output\fR] [\fB\-\-url\fR] [\fB\-\-txt\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-passphrase\fR] [\fB\-\-passphrase\-file\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Unlock a key file and print its armored public key
(\-\-\-\-\-BEGIN HS PUBLIC KEY\-\-\-\-\-) for out\-of\-band distribution or for serving
at a well\-known URL. The private key is never exported — it stays in the
encrypted .hskey file.
.PP
With \-\-txt \-\-url <URL>, emit the DNS pin record instead:
HSPIN:SHA3\-256:<fingerprint>:<url>. Publish that single short line as the
_hs_key.<host> TXT record and serve the armored public key at <url>;
remote verification downloads the key and requires its fingerprint to
match the pin.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-k\fR, \fB\-\-key\fR \fI<KEY>\fR
Path to the secret key file (.hskey)
.TP
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-output\fR \fI<OUTPUT>\fR
Write the public key to this file
.TP
\fB\-\-url\fR \fI<URL>\fR
URL of the public key to publish in the _hs_key DNS pin record
.TP
\fB\-\-txt\fR
Output the HSPIN:SHA3\-256:<fingerprint>:<url> DNS TXT record (requires \-\-url)
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-passphrase\fR
Use an empty passphrase (no prompt)
.TP
\fB\-\-passphrase\-file\fR \fI<PASSPHRASE_FILE>\fR
Read the passphrase from a file (first line)
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
